# The guarded service default under the target-gated route
# (docs/journal/2026-11-10-service-guarded-target-gated-registration.md).
# DRAFT: not frozen. A freeze sets, in its own commit and nothing else:
#   candidate <40-hex>      the commit whose build and workload inputs HEAD must match
#   base <40-hex>           master as fetched at the freeze, merged into the candidate
#   base_fetched <UTC>      YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ, when that master was fetched
#   rustc <rustc -V>        the workstation's toolchain, exactly as `rustc -V` prints it there
#   ni_rustc <rustc -V>     the CI shards' toolchain, as `rustc -V` prints it (the dispatch's
#                           `toolchain` input selects it)
#   corpus_text <sha256>    the `text` corpus's digest: ab gen builds it from the candidate's
#                           own sources (the other six are bench/service_tg.py's CORPUS_SHA256)
# Until then `just bench-service-tg` refuses, and bench/service_tg.py admits nothing.
